  "claim": "The director of Finding Dory co-directed the film A Bug's Life.",
  "evidencia": "Page: Andrew Stanton. Sentence: His film work includes writing and directing Pixar's \"A Bug's Life\" (1998) (as co-director), \"Finding Nemo\" (2003), and \"WALL-E\" (2008), and the live-action film, Disney's \"John Carter\" (2012).\nPage: A Bug's Life. Sentence: Directed by John Lasseter, the film involves a misfit ant named Flik that is looking for \"tough warriors\" to save his colony from greedy grasshoppers, only to recruit a group of bugs that turn out to be an inept circus troupe.\nPage: Finding Dory. Sentence: Directed by Andrew Stanton with co-direction by Angus MacLane, the screenplay was written by Stanton and Victoria Strouse.",
