        "original_id": "a2507c7d-2253-5cdd-9f44-6e8ed9f75e23",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Andrew Stanton, John Lasseter, Angus MacLane, Victoria Strouse\n- Films: A Bug's Life, Finding Nemo, WALL-E, John Carter, Finding Dory\n- Companies: Pixar, Disney\n\nFacts:\n- In 1998, Andrew Stanton co-directed Pixar's film A Bug's Life.\n- A Bug's Life was directed by John Lasseter.\n- A Bug's Life follows a misfit ant named Flik, who seeks tough warriors to save his colony from greedy grasshoppers and instead recruits an inept circus troupe of bugs.\n- In 2003, Andrew Stanton wrote and directed Pixar's Finding Nemo.\n- In 2008, Andrew Stanton wrote and directed Pixar's WALL-E.\n- In 2012, Andrew Stanton wrote and directed Disney's live-action film John Carter.\n- Finding Dory was directed by Andrew Stanton with co-direction by Angus MacLane.\n- The screenplay for Finding Dory was written by Andrew Stanton and Victoria Strouse.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "936eef1b-a7e5-5072-8aa5-fba38c4335ac",
        "text": "Page: Andrew Stanton. Sentence: His film work includes writing and directing Pixar's \"A Bug's Life\" (1998) (as co-director), \"Finding Nemo\" (2003), and \"WALL-E\" (2008), and the live-action film, Disney's \"John Carter\" (2012).\nPage: A Bug's Life. Sentence: Directed by John Lasseter, the film involves a misfit ant named Flik that is looking for \"tough warriors\" to save his colony from greedy grasshoppers, only to recruit a group of bugs that turn out to be an inept circus troupe.\nPage: Finding Dory. Sentence: Directed by Andrew Stanton with co-direction by Angus MacLane, the screenplay was written by Stanton and Victoria Strouse.",
